# MCP Agent Architecture

The Multi-tool Conversational Program (MCP) agent is based on LangGraph and handles specialized queries through dedicated servers.

## Agent Components

- [src/agent/client.py](mdc:src/agent/client.py) - MCP agent client implementation

## MCP Servers

The MCP architecture uses specialized servers for different query types:

- [src/mcp_servers/math_server.py](mdc:src/mcp_servers/math_server.py) - Server for handling mathematical calculations
- [src/mcp_servers/weather_server.py](mdc:src/mcp_servers/weather_server.py) - Server for handling weather-related queries

## Client Implementations

- [client.py](mdc:client.py) - Standard client for local usage
- [lambda_client.py](mdc:lambda_client.py) - Client implementation for AWS Lambda
- [lambda_client_adapter.py](mdc:lambda_client_adapter.py) - Adapter layer for the Lambda client

## Testing

- [test_queries.py](mdc:test_queries.py) - Sample test queries for the MCP agent
- [run_tests.py](mdc:run_tests.py) - Script to run tests against the MCP agent

## Integration with Frontend

The MCP agent receives queries via the Flask backend which uses Socket.IO to communicate with the frontend application.
